moving on now to the aftermath of that  racist attack in buffalo which killed 10  people and caused shock sadness and  outrage all across the country president  biden visited the community yesterday  and called the mass shooting an act of  quote domestic terrorism he urged  americans to reject white supremacy and  the conspiracy theories that inspired  the alleged gunman  and the president spent more than an  hour with families of the victims our  national correspondent duncan was there  for the president's visit has been there  since sunday in fact rica good morning  to you how did people respond to the  president's speech  good morning to you all at the table the  president was needed here in terms of  the families who've lost loved ones but  there was a feeling a mixed feeling if  you will about his visit uh take some  video here that we're going to show you  hundreds of people were gathered outside  of that community center where he spoke  to the families of those killed some  were outside praying and kneeling in a  moment of reflection while others were  screaming and chanting get off your  knees and stand up and fight  white supremacy is a poison  it's a poison  speaking to a grieving community tuesday  an emotional president biden condemned  the racist ideology of the accused  gunman who killed 10 black people at  this buffalo supermarket i call on all  americans to reject the lie and i  condemn those who spread the lie for  power  political gain  and for profit the president was calling  out those who have pushed the great  replacement theory the belief apparently  shared by the accused shooter that white  americans are being systematically  replaced by immigrants and minorities  roberta drury 32 beloved daughter and  sister the president named each of the  victims andre mcneil  53  worked at a restaurant went to buy his  three-year-old son a birthday cake after  a speech the president hugged macneal's  three-year-old son and gave him a  presidential challenge coin his family  said he's too young to understand what  happened to his father my uncle's story  and what happened to him wasn't just  kicked under a rug like it meant nothing  because it meant a lot theon and linda  elliott are andre mcneil's brother and  niece for people who are angry and are  talking about  there needs to be retaliation what do  you say to that i say do i say you're  only dividing don't do that that's not  good every person that is of caucasian  or black or whatever is not evil many  families are still recovering from that  horrific shooting eight-year-old london  thomas was with her parents when shots  rang out i was scared for my mom because  i thought something happened to her she  and her dad split up from her mom and  rushed to the back of the store they  barricaded themselves inside a mill  cooler until they could be rescued i  didn't know what's going on i just like  followed my dad her mom julie hartwell  is stuck wondering the same questions  many in this community are facing this  morning what are we going to do  after this  that's all i'm worried about  because my kid has to grow up  here  what is the next step  to prevent this from even happening  anymore  president biden acknowledged that  there's little he can do to take on gun  reform when it comes through passing  anything through executive action he  said that he needed to convince congress  to go back to what he was able to help  pass as a u.s senator in the 90s  referring to that 10-year ban on assault  weapons which some have deemed  controversial and have questioned  whether or not something like that would  actually make a difference when it comes  to the mass shootings that have been  committed over the last decade  nate  thank you so much we know that the pain  is just starting and the healing will  begin hopefully soon
 

